      "side": 1,
      "message": "Clearing `VNET_BUFFER_F_GSO` and falling through to regular SEND does not actually segment the packet. Since the interface advertises TCP GSO, software segmentation has already been bypassed, so this can transmit the GSO super-packet as one oversized frame. Should these fallback cases be dropped or explicitly software-segmented instead?",
      "revId": "faff551fb82b7ee9e8e5e0b675c4156782cf6701",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
