      "writtenOn": "2026-07-06T13:14:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skipping a zero-length fragment here can leak it when `dseg` is at a WQEBB boundary. The preceding code removes the parent\u0027s `NEXT` link and records the child in `txq-\u003ebufs`; because `chained_n` is not incremented, the next iteration reuses that slot and can overwrite the zero-length child\u0027s index. Can we skip empty fragments without changing the ownership chain, or otherwise preserve their buffer index for completion cleanup?",
      "revId": "faff551fb82b7ee9e8e5e0b675c4156782cf6701",
